# Implementation Plan - Spring Boot 3 HRM (Human Resource Management) Modulith

Design and implement a production-grade, enterprise-level **Spring Boot 3 Modular Monolith (Spring Modulith)** backend application for Human Resource Management (HRMS). The application follows Domain-Driven Design (DDD) principles with well-encapsulated modules, asynchronous/transactional event-driven inter-module communication, Spring Modulith architectural verification and automated documentation generation, Spring Security JWT authentication, and full REST API parity with the Angular HRMS frontend.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Location**: The backend will be initialized in `hrms-backend/` inside the workspace root (`d:\JITENDRA_SHUKLA\HRMS\hrms-backend`).
> - **Technology Stack**:
>   - **Java 21** & **Spring Boot 3.4.x** (or 3.3.x)
>   - **Spring Modulith 1.3.x** (`spring-modulith-starter-core`, `spring-modulith-starter-jpa`, `spring-modulith-starter-test`, `spring-modulith-docs`)
>   - **Spring Data JPA** & **H2 Database** (with PostgreSQL / MySQL production profiles)
>   - **Spring Security 6** with **Stateless JWT Authentication** & RBAC (`SUPER_ADMIN`, `COMPANY_ADMIN`, `HR_MANAGER`, `EMPLOYEE`)
>   - **SpringDoc OpenAPI 3 / Swagger UI** for interactive API documentation
>   - **Spring Modulith Event Publication Registry** for guaranteed event delivery
>   - **Maven** as the build management tool

> [!NOTE]
> All modules are designed with strict Spring Modulith boundaries: internal implementation classes reside in `.internal` packages or are package-private, while module APIs, DTOs, and Domain Events are exposed in the root module packages.

